/*
RMSTEST_37 - WHICH zone does set_zone_by_team give an un-teamed player
preview-design.md Sec.15 item 14, third attempt - PROXIMITY IS NOW FORCED

WHY 29 AND 34 BOTH FAILED, AND THEY FAILED DIFFERENTLY
RMSTEST_29 returned eight separate patches, which both surviving hypotheses
predict, so it could not discriminate. RMSTEST_34 added probe lands at the two
boundary zones - and came back with every probe, INCLUDING THE CONTROL, sitting
17 to 21 tiles from the player lands. Nothing separated them.

RMSTEST_34's own prediction 4 named that outcome in advance: sharing a zone only
PERMITS contact, it does not compel it. A probe land placed at random has to
happen to grow next to the one player land it might share a zone with, and on a
200 map with eight players it simply never did. The asymmetry was in the header
and the design still leaned on the weak half of it.

So this attempt stops sampling and starts arranging. direct_placement pins
player 1 at a known tile and every probe goes at a known offset from it. Contact
is then decided by the zone rule alone, because the geometry is fixed.

THE HYPOTHESES, both about PLAYER 1 specifically
  A  PINNED CHOICE. Un-teamed keeps the default player zone, playerNumber - 10.
     Player 1 is in zone -9.
  B  Every player carries an engine-internal TeamNumber even when solo, so the
     zone is TeamNumber - 9 with no special case. Player 1 is in zone -8.

Note this corrects RMSTEST_34's probe choice. That script probed -9 and -1, on
the reasoning that -1 is player 8's zone under B - but it pinned nothing about
where player 8 was, so the -1 probe was untestable even in principle. Both
probes here are aimed at PLAYER 1, whose position is fixed.

METHOD
  player 1   GRASS  at tile (100,100), set_zone_by_team
  probe A    DIRT   at tile (100, 78), zone -9   shares with P1 under A only
  probe B    DESERT at tile (100,122), zone -8   shares with P1 under B only
  control    DIRT3  at tile ( 78,100), zone  5   shares under NEITHER

Every probe origin is 22 tiles from player 1's origin - far enough that
min_placement_distance cannot reject it, close enough that a land of this size
reaches player 1's edge in a few growth rounds if nothing stops it. With
other_zone_avoidance_distance 20, a probe in a DIFFERENT zone is pushed away and
grows outward instead; a probe SHARING the zone grows straight into contact.

READ IT WITH
  python probe_scenario.py "<scenario>" --patches GRASS
  plus minimum distance from each probe terrain to the GRASS land.
  The reading is WHICH probe is in contact. Contact means roughly 0 to 5 tiles;
  pushed-away means at or above 20.

PREDICTIONS, RECORDED BEFORE THE RUN
1. Under A: DIRT in contact with GRASS, DESERT at or above 20. Sec.6.1's pinned
   choice becomes a measurement and the special case stays.
2. Under B: DESERT in contact, DIRT at or above 20. Sec.6.1 loses the special
   case entirely - an un-teamed player's zone is TeamNumber - 9 like everyone
   else - and the model gets simpler.
3. DIRT3 must be at or above 20 in every run. IT IS THE CONTROL. If it makes
   contact, other_zone_avoidance_distance is not separating anything at these
   distances and neither probe can be read - which is exactly the state
   RMSTEST_34 ended in, and the reason this script exists.
4. If BOTH DIRT and DESERT make contact, the zone rule is not exclusive and
   neither hypothesis is right as stated. Record it; that would be a third
   finding rather than a failed run.

The instrument is now symmetric: contact and non-contact are both forced by the
geometry, so unlike RMSTEST_34 a null result actually means something.

GENERATE AT NORMAL (200) WITH 8 PLAYERS, ALL UN-TEAMED (plain FFA, no team
setup, no lobby needed). RUN IT THREE TIMES.

Note direct_placement means players 2-8 get no land at all - that is intended.
Only player 1's zone is under test, and the seven absent lands remove every
other thing that could have pushed a probe around.
*/

<PLAYER_SETUP>
  direct_placement

<LAND_GENERATION>
  base_terrain SNOW

  /* Player 1, pinned. set_zone_by_team is the attribute under test. */
  create_land
  {
    terrain_type GRASS
    number_of_tiles 200
    base_size 5
    clumping_factor 20
    border_fuzziness 0
    land_position 50 50
    assign_to AT_PLAYER 1 0 0
    set_zone_by_team
    other_zone_avoidance_distance 20
  }

  /* probe A - player 1's zone under hypothesis A */
  create_land
  {
    terrain_type DIRT
    number_of_tiles 200
    base_size 5
    clumping_factor 20
    border_fuzziness 0
    land_position 50 39
    zone -9
    other_zone_avoidance_distance 20
  }

  /* probe B - player 1's zone under hypothesis B */
  create_land
  {
    terrain_type DESERT
    number_of_tiles 200
    base_size 5
    clumping_factor 20
    border_fuzziness 0
    land_position 50 61
    zone -8
    other_zone_avoidance_distance 20
  }

  /* CONTROL - nobody's zone under either hypothesis. Must NOT make contact. */
  create_land
  {
    terrain_type DIRT3
    number_of_tiles 200
    base_size 5
    clumping_factor 20
    border_fuzziness 0
    land_position 39 50
    zone 5
    other_zone_avoidance_distance 20
  }

<ELEVATION_GENERATION>

/* NO <CLIFF_GENERATION> HEADER - an empty one generates cliffs. */

<TERRAIN_GENERATION>

<OBJECTS_GENERATION>

<CONNECTION_GENERATION>
